AIM:
To find approximate solution for vertex cover problem.

Algorithm:
Read number of vertices and edges
Initialize all vertices as not covered
Pick an uncovered edge (u,v)
Add u and v to vertex cover
Remove all edges incident on u and v
Repeat until no edges left
Print vertex cover

PROGRAM:
#include<stdio.h>
int main()
{
    int n,i,j;
    int graph[10][10];
    int visited[10]={0};
    printf("Enter number of vertices: ");
    scanf("%d",&n);
    printf("Enter adjacency matrix:\n");
    for(i=0;i<n;i++)
        for(j=0;j<n;j++)
            scanf("%d",&graph[i][j]);
    for(i=0;i<n;i++)
    {
        for(j=0;j<n;j++)
        {
            if(graph[i][j] && !visited[i] && !visited[j])
            {
                visited[i]=visited[j]=1;
            }
        }
    }
    printf("Vertex cover:\n");
    for(i=0;i<n;i++)
        if(visited[i])
            printf("%d ",i);
}

OUTPUT:
